<p> List of all output redshifts for all the simulations present in the
database. Note that SQL queries are made easier by the use of the snapshot
number rather than the redshift. Lookback times are given in Gigayears. </p>

<table>     
  <tr><th>column</th><th>type</th><th>UCD</th><th>unit</th><th>description</th></tr>

	<tr>
	  <td>Snapnum</td>
	  <td>int</td>
	  <td></td>
	  <td>-</td>
	  <td>Snapshot number<br></td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
	  <td>Redshift</td>
	  <td>Float</td>
	  <td></td>
	  <td>-</td>
	  <td>The redshift of this snapshot</td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
	  <td>LookbackTime</td>
	  <td>Float</td>
	  <td></td>
	  <td>Gyr</td>
	  <td>The look back time for this snapshot<br></td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
	  <td>LumDistance</td>
	  <td>Float</td>
	  <td></td>
	  <td>Mpc</td>
	  <td>Luminosity distance D<sub>L</sub><br></td>
	</tr>

</table>

